From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:28:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Autosave players that were never saved

lastSave starts at LAST_SAVE_ABSENT (Long.MIN_VALUE), and the autosave
check computes now - lastSave, which overflows to a negative number. A
player is therefore only autosaved after something else (a manual
save-all, a world change) saved them once, so a crash loses everything
done since join.

Based on PaperMC/Folia#459 (Dueris)

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java b/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
index 5869785258d2ec7483ed11275f4abc072068e74b..2bb63bb31788b76c08813803a4fe73688cc4e0de 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
@@ -1049,7 +1049,7 @@ public abstract class PlayerList {
                 continue;
             }
             // Folia end - region threading
-            if (interval == -1 || now - player.lastSave >= timeInterval) { // Folia - region threading
+            if (interval == -1 || player.lastSave == ServerPlayer.LAST_SAVE_ABSENT || now - player.lastSave >= timeInterval) { // Folia - region threading // Tessera - now - Long.MIN_VALUE overflows, so unsaved players were never autosaved
                 profiler.startTimer(ca.spottedleaf.leafprofiler.LProfilerRegistry.PLAYER_SAVE); try { // Folia - profiler
                 this.save(player);
                 } finally { profiler.stopTimer(ca.spottedleaf.leafprofiler.LProfilerRegistry.PLAYER_SAVE); } // Folia - profiler
